  "notes": "\"The harmony is the parameter\" — the entry's own words for a working songwriter's vocabulary: \"maj7/m9/13 voicings, real 4-to-8-bar cycles with secondary dominants, gospel passing chords, and modulation. Blues harmony where the guitar leads.\" So `maxChords` is 6, a `ii–V–I` and a blues `I–IV–V` sit beside the minor cycles, the triad share is low and `susOrDimProb` carries the passing chords. ⛔ **`bass808` is null**: \"played electric bass with syncopated funk motion as the default, doubled by a short sub; long sliding 808s appear only on the rap collaborations.\" The kit is the entry's hybrid — \"a live-feel or convincingly-humanised kit with the backbeat on 2&4 and ghost 16ths, layered with a programmed 808 kick and finger-snaps\" — so the snare ghosts heavily, the grid is loose, and the perc block carries snaps. \"He produces, writes, plays and sings, so the arrangement arrives whole\" is the full-song structure with an instrumental solo section; the vocal \"arranged like a horn section\" is a high counter ratio, and the \"rasped edge… high note-density, gospel runs\" is the melody's density and register. ⚠ `confidence` is **low**, mirroring the entry's medium-low: \"his multi-instrumentalist/songwriter role is sourced; the parametric detail is inference from the records\". ⚠ All drum, swing and bassline numbers are **INFERRED**. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research.",
